1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,447
This is LEOTherm version one point two point ten. Start in Quick start. Chinese and English use the same model and
solver; language only changes the interface, plots and report.

2
00:00:12,447 --> 00:00:20,743
In the goal dropdown, select Paper: reference task and 36 cases. You do not need to enter model parameters
individually. This entry uses the fixed paper protocol and runs the reference task, all 36 conditions and three

3
00:00:20,743 --> 00:00:29,039
time-refinement cases.

4
00:00:29,039 --> 00:00:38,869
Click Reproduce paper and report. Choose a parent folder for the outputs. The software creates a new task subfolder
without overwriting previous results. Wait for the computations and report export to finish. Computation time is

5
00:00:38,869 --> 00:00:48,700
omitted here. On completion, the report opens in the current language.

6
00:00:48,700 --> 00:00:59,642
The reference task covers two hours with a 60-second output interval and no warmup. The 36-case study combines
three orbital altitudes, four target beta angles and three effective thermal conductances between the structure and RF

7
00:00:59,642 --> 00:01:10,585
front end. Each case is initialized periodically before six orbits are analyzed. Keep this separate from the reference-task
initial transient.

8
00:01:10,585 --> 00:01:18,938
The eleven-node network distinguishes six exterior faces, the structure, antenna and receiver electronics. The matrix
records effective thermal conductance in watts per kelvin. The study changes only the structure-to-RF link; all other

9
00:01:18,938 --> 00:01:27,291
equipment parameters stay fixed.

10
00:01:27,291 --> 00:01:36,049
The combined study report is in the report folder of the new task directory. It includes reference temperatures,
absorbed external power, conductive paths, 36-case curves and paired comparisons. Both language reports come from

11
00:01:36,049 --> 00:01:44,807
the same results; a separate simulation is not needed.

12
00:01:44,807 --> 00:01:57,059
The upper panels compare RF temperature P95 minus P5; the lower panels compare orbital-frequency phase delay
relative to total absorbed external power. The temperature difference ranges from about 0.995 to 6.048 kelvin.

13
00:01:57,059 --> 00:02:09,311
Increasing conductance increases fluctuations in eclipsing cases, reduces them under continuous sunlight, and shortens
phase delay in all twelve orbital pairs.

14
00:02:09,311 --> 00:02:19,596
Check that the task status is complete and the case count is 36. Then inspect the audit and time-refinement tables.
Cases two, twenty and thirty-six are independently recomputed at twice the output resolution. The report shows the

15
00:02:19,596 --> 00:02:29,881
measured differences. Full temperature histories are retained in open_data for independent checking.

16
00:02:29,881 --> 00:02:39,689
With MATLAB, use the source command shown here. Without a MATLAB license, install the free R2021b Runtime and
use the paper-study argument of the new executable. The output directory must be new. If execution stops, inspect the

17
00:02:39,689 --> 00:02:49,497
stage and error in the status file before rerunning into a fresh directory.